# Accessibility

## Semantic HTML first

- `<button>` for actions, `<a>` for navigation — never `<div onClick>`
- `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<aside>`, `<header>`, `<footer>` for landmarks
- heading hierarchy (`h1` > `h2` > `h3`) — never skip levels for styling
- `<ul>`/`<ol>` for lists — screen readers announce item counts

## ARIA

- add ARIA only when semantic HTML is insufficient
- `aria-label` on icon-only buttons: `<Button aria-label="Close dialog">`
- `aria-describedby` for inputs with help text or errors
- `aria-live="polite"` for dynamic content (toasts, status changes)
- `role="status"` for loading indicators

## Keyboard

- every interactive element focusable + operable via keyboard
- visible focus rings — never `outline-none` without `focus-visible:ring-2`
- focus trap in modals — shadcn Dialog/Sheet/Drawer handles this
- `Escape` closes modals/popovers/dropdowns — shadcn handles this

## Forms

- every input has a visible `<Label>` — shadcn `<Label htmlFor="...">`
- group related fields with `<fieldset>` + `<legend>`
- error messages linked via `aria-describedby` — never color-only
- required fields: `aria-required="true"` or native `required`

## Images + icons

- `<img>` always has `alt`; decorative → `alt=""`
- icons next to text are decorative: `aria-hidden="true"`
- icon-only controls always carry `aria-label`

## Rules

- color is never the only indicator — pair with icon, text, or pattern
- touch targets minimum 44×44px on mobile
- test with keyboard-only navigation before shipping
- never rely on hover to reveal primary affordances
